<style>
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .shinobi-wrapper{background:#e6dfcf;background-image:radial-gradient(circle at 100% 50%,rgba(0,0,0,.05),transparent 50%),radial-gradient(circle at 0 0,rgba(200,180,150,.4),transparent 40%);padding:20px;height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;color:#332b22;overflow:auto}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .top-title-area h1{font-family:'Kaushan Script',Georgia,serif;font-size:36px;border:0;margin:0;color:#1a1510}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .header-grid-area{display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:center;margin:12px 0}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .profile-section img{width:125px;height:125px;object-fit:cover;border:3px solid #7d644a;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-heading{flex:1}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .sheet-tabs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px;margin:12px 0;border-bottom:2px solid #79654b}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .sheet-tabs .item{padding:9px 13px;background:#d2c2a5;border:1px solid #9e886b;border-radius:5px 5px 0 0;color:#332b22;font-weight:bold}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .sheet-tabs .item.active{background:#fff3d8}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .sheet-body{flex:1;overflow:auto;min-height:0}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-panel{background:rgba(255,255,255,.4);border:1px solid #ab9677;padding:12px;margin:10px 0;border-radius:5px}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-stat-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(170px,1fr));gap:10px}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-stat{background:#f4ebda;border:1px solid #bba587;border-radius:4px;padding:10px}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-stat strong{display:block;font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-stat span{font-size:23px;font-weight:bold}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-actions{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:10px 0}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-actions button{width:auto;flex:1;min-width:135px}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-device-row{border:1px solid #ab9677;border-radius:5px;margin:10px 0;background:#f4ebda;padding:12px}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet .puppet-device-row summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:bold}
.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet input,.shinobi.sheet.actor.puppet select{color:#332b22}
</style>
<form autocomplete="off" class="shinobi-wrapper">
<div class="top-title-area"><h1>Kugutsu — Puppet Sheet</h1></div>
<div class="header-grid-area">
 <div class="profile-section"><img src="{{puppetImage}}" data-edit="img" title="Edit Puppet Portrait"></div>
 <div class="puppet-heading"><h2><input name="name" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" aria-label="Puppet Name"></h2><p><strong>Initial Puppet</strong> · {{puppet.size}} · Hijutsu Vol. 2</p>
 <label>Controller <select name="flags.shinobi-no-sho-revamp.puppetProfile.controllerId"><option value="">Not assigned</option>{{#each controllers}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
 <p>Controlled by: <strong>{{controllerName}}</strong></p></div>
</div>
<nav class="sheet-tabs tabs" data-group="primary"><a class="item" data-tab="overview">Overview</a><a class="item" data-tab="combat">Combat</a><a class="item" data-tab="devices">Equipment & Devices</a><a class="item" data-tab="rules">Puppet Rules</a></nav>
<section class="sheet-body">
<div class="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="overview"><div class="puppet-panel">
<p>Controller: {{controllerName}}. Attacks and defenses below read the controller’s current sheet.</p>{{#unless hasController}}<p>Assign a controller before play. The first assignment initializes Absorption from their Mechanics.</p>{{/unless}}{{#if disabled}}<p><strong>UNUSABLE — 0 Absorption. Requires repair.</strong></p>{{/if}}
<table><tr><th>Mechanics</th><td>{{stats.mechanics}}</td><th>Body Hardness</th><td>{{stats.hardness}}</td></tr><tr><th>Maximum Absorption</th><td>{{stats.absorptionMax}}</td><th>Remaining</th><td><input type="number" min="0" max="{{stats.absorptionMax}}" name="flags.shinobi-no-sho-revamp.puppetProfile.absorptionRemaining" value="{{remaining}}"></td></tr><tr><th>Attack (Ranged Combat)</th><td>{{stats.attack}}</td><th>Dodge / Anticipate</th><td>{{stats.dodge}} / {{stats.anticipate}}</td></tr><tr><th>Control range</th><td>{{stats.controlRange}} m</td><th>Device ranged reach</th><td>{{stats.attackRange}} m</td></tr></table>
<div class="puppet-actions"><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="attack">Roll Attack</button><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="dodge">Roll Dodge</button><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="anticipate">Roll Anticipate</button><button type="button" class="puppet-repair">Complete 4-hour Repair</button></div>
<p><strong>Example aptitudes:</strong> {{aptitudesText}}. These are the book’s sample purchases for this puppet. Allocate the controller’s power points and meet normal prerequisites; their bonuses are not automatically added to these rolls.</p><div class="puppet-panel"><h3>Construction</h3><p><strong>Size:</strong> {{puppet.size}} · <strong>Carrying:</strong> {{construction.carry}} · <strong>Skeleton:</strong> {{construction.skeletonCost}} Ryō · <strong>Initial build cost:</strong> {{puppet.materialsCost}} Ryō</p><p><strong>Light slots:</strong> {{construction.used.Light}} / {{construction.capacity.Light}} · <strong>Standard slots:</strong> {{construction.used.Standard}} / {{construction.capacity.Standard}} · <strong>Heavy slots:</strong> {{construction.used.Heavy}} / {{construction.capacity.Heavy}}</p>{{#unless construction.valid}}<p><strong>Warning: Installed devices exceed slot capacity or duplicate a Heavy device.</strong></p>{{/unless}}<p>Slot prices: Light 10, Standard 20, Heavy 30 Ryō. Three Standard slots may be exchanged for one Heavy slot; larger slots may be replaced with smaller ones. Changes to slot layout and installed devices require the Repair action.</p><p>Increase puppet size for 300 Ryō per size, decrease size for free, and sell puppets or slots for half price. Creating an actor does not deduct money.</p></div></div></div>
<div class="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="combat"><div class="puppet-panel"><h2>Combat Actions</h2><p>Attack and defenses use the controller's statistics. Puppet Absorption is tracked independently.</p><div class="puppet-stat-grid"><div class="puppet-stat"><strong>Ranged Combat</strong><span>{{stats.attack}}</span></div><div class="puppet-stat"><strong>Dodge</strong><span>{{stats.dodge}}</span></div><div class="puppet-stat"><strong>Anticipate</strong><span>{{stats.anticipate}}</span></div><div class="puppet-stat"><strong>Body Hardness</strong><span>{{stats.hardness}}</span></div></div><div class="puppet-actions"><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="attack">Roll Attack</button><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="dodge">Roll Dodge</button><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="anticipate">Roll Anticipate</button></div><h3>Weapon Attacks</h3>{{#each devices}}{{#if canAttack}}<div class="puppet-device-row"><strong>{{name}}</strong> — Base damage {{baseDamage}} <button type="button" class="puppet-device-attack" data-item-id="{{id}}">Roll Attack</button></div>{{/if}}{{/each}}</div></div>
<div class="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="devices"><div class="puppet-panel"><h2>Installed Equipment & Devices</h2><button type="button" class="puppet-refill">Village Resupply — Restore Device Uses</button>{{#each devices}}<details class="puppet-device-row" open><summary><strong>{{name}}</strong> — {{slot}}</summary><button type="button" class="puppet-open-device" data-item-id="{{id}}">Open Item Sheet</button>{{#if canAttack}}<p><button type="button" class="puppet-device-attack" data-item-id="{{id}}">Roll {{name}} Attack</button></p><p>Weapon Damage +{{weaponDamage}} · Base damage {{baseDamage}} = ceil(Mechanics / 2 + Weapon Damage).</p>{{/if}}{{#if limited}}<p>Remaining uses: {{remainingUses}} / {{maxUses}} <button type="button" class="puppet-use-charge" data-item-id="{{id}}">Spend One Use</button></p>{{/if}}{{#if minimumMechanics}}<p>Requires Mechanics {{minimumMechanics}}. {{#if locked}}<strong>Prerequisite not met.</strong>{{/if}}</p>{{/if}}<p style="white-space:pre-line">{{description}}</p></details>{{/each}}<p>Device activations normally use a Standard Action. Handle device-specific chakra, areas, poison, effects and aptitude modifiers manually; spending a use only updates its remaining charge.</p></div></div>
<div class="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="rules"><div class="puppet-panel"><p>Puppets are constructed weapons, separate from animal Kuchiyose. Puppets have Body Hardness 1 and Absorption 5 × the controller’s Mechanics, modified by −5 for Small or +5 for Large. At 0 Absorption they become unusable; a Tool Kit and 4-hour repair by their puppeteer restores them at no additional material cost. They do not use creature Vitality, NC allocation or half-Vitality rules.</p><p>Puppet actions and devices do not normally consume chakra unless a specific rule states otherwise. Check the separate chakra-thread connection rules when establishing control. Drawing a puppet is a Free Action. Base control range: 10m + 2m per Spirit; ranged device reach: 5m + Spirit. Transfer the controller’s Movement or Standard Action for puppet movement or attacks. Kurohigi determines how many puppets may be connected/acted with; creating actor copies does not increase that limit.</p><p>All attacks use the controller’s Ranged Combat, including melee maneuvers. Use the controller’s Dodge/Anticipate for defense. Apply their relevant condition penalties and camouflage. Manual skill checks for Agility/Dexterity tasks use the controller’s Sleight of Hand. The puppet must be visible to its controller.</p><p>Fear, fascination and fatigue do not affect the puppet as a human, but movement restrictions can. An uncontrolled puppet is a defenseless object. Rules for chakra threads, compatible aptitudes, control limits, winged targets, maneuvers and other Kugutsu features remain in force.</p><p>This sheet tracks Absorption and device uses, and rolls controller precision. It does not automatically pay exceptional chakra costs, enforce turn actions, install upgrades, place summoned tokens or apply damage. Drag this actor to a scene for a selectable token. The token hides ordinary character Vitality bars to avoid confusing them with puppet Absorption.</p></div></div>
</section></form>
